==Enemy==
One of the most powerful Alien peons, Mesocosmocyclone is essentially a frailer but more aggressive [[Super Cosmic Cyclone]] that [[Warp|warps]] Cats forward instead of backward. Mesocosmocyclone's only weakness of note is its very low range, so when it gets hit by status effects repeatedly, it stops pushing.

Despite appearing to be levitate, it isn't a Floating enemy.

==Strategy==
'''DO NOT UNDERESTIMATE THIS ENEMY!''' Remember that Mesocosmocyclone, while small, is still a [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]], so its DPS and attack rate are off the charts. You will want to kill this thing as fast as possible before it shreds through your frontlines. [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] are ideal for dealing with it, provided they are decently leveled.

[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]] will help a lot when fighting this enemy, but it will still only last a couple of seconds. At high levels, the [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall]] or [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Thunderbolt]] can halt its movement for a few seconds.

[[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] is a very good and consistent option as a crowd-controller, as he can impede Mesocosmocyclone's advance from long range so your other attackers can burst it down. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] can do the same, but it is recommended you invest in his [[Talents]] to improve his reliability.

